WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.057 --> 00:00:05.303
(bouncy music)

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.128
- [Voiceover] This looks crazy.

00:00:11.128 --> 00:00:11.744
- It does.

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:13.045
It looks like, this looks like something

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:14.644
you would have 3D printed.

00:00:14.644 --> 00:00:15.314
- What is this?

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:16.883
Spicy roasted fish crackers.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.968
- Ugh!

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:18.766
- These are your daily snacks.

00:00:18.766 --> 00:00:20.220
- Ugh!

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.124
It smells like a bait and tackle shop.

00:00:24.376 --> 00:00:25.851
- Ooh, it's spicier than I thought.

00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:26.935
- I don't like it.

00:00:26.935 --> 00:00:27.512
- I like it!

00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:28.770
- I don't taste the fish at all, actually.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.772
- Does Indonesia know
what fish tastes like?

00:00:30.772 --> 00:00:31.941
- I don't...

00:00:31.941 --> 00:00:33.408
- They just smack fish on things and go,

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:34.527
like, yeah, sure.

00:00:36.171 --> 00:00:39.374
- Chiki. Chiki Balls.

00:00:39.374 --> 00:00:41.491
They're not afraid to use balls.

00:00:41.491 --> 00:00:43.308
- Chiki Balls.

00:00:43.308 --> 00:00:45.245
Do chickens have balls?

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.788
- Dude, it says balls.

00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:48.290
- Actually, all it says is balls.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:51.076
- It's like, it's a baby
chicken, eat my balls!

00:00:51.076 --> 00:00:51.918
- Oh God.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.711
- That's what he's saying.

00:00:52.711 --> 00:00:54.462
- It's like a ball of dirt and cheese.

00:00:54.462 --> 00:00:55.964
- Are they cheese or are they chicken?

00:00:55.964 --> 00:00:57.216
- That's exactly what I
thought it would taste like.

00:00:57.216 --> 00:00:57.924
- I mean--

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:58.874
- That guy's balls.

00:00:58.874 --> 00:00:59.552
I mean...

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.555
- Taro Net.

00:01:02.555 --> 00:01:04.221
It looks like a net.

00:01:04.221 --> 00:01:05.307
Made of seaweed.

00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:06.767
- This is like a real savory flavor.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.518
It tastes almost like olives and pickles.

00:01:08.518 --> 00:01:10.312
Not like pickles, but like olives.

00:01:10.312 --> 00:01:11.855
Like olive oil.

00:01:11.855 --> 00:01:13.273
- It tastes like seaweed crackers.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.900
- It smells like Play-Doh.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.235
- It does smell like Play-Doh.

00:01:17.235 --> 00:01:18.904
But it doesn't taste like Play-doh,

00:01:18.904 --> 00:01:21.365
and I know that 'cause
I used to eat Play-Doh.

00:01:21.365 --> 00:01:23.492
- Everyone did. You're not special.

00:01:23.492 --> 00:01:26.045
- [Voiceover] Cassava is also a root?

00:01:26.045 --> 00:01:26.796
- [Voiceover] Yeah.

00:01:26.796 --> 00:01:28.872
- Do you guys just not
have potatoes in Indonesia?

00:01:28.872 --> 00:01:29.831
- Oh my man.

00:01:29.831 --> 00:01:30.791
I'm not even going to
be able to taste this.

00:01:30.791 --> 00:01:31.917
My mouth's already on fire.

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.004
- This is delicious.

00:01:34.004 --> 00:01:34.836
- It is delicious.

00:01:34.836 --> 00:01:36.129
How many calories are in this?

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.914
- What does this taste like?

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.339
- It tastes like cereal.

00:01:41.339 --> 00:01:43.136
- 95 in--

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.095
- 95 calories.

00:01:44.095 --> 00:01:46.390
- In 0.9 ounces?!

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.724
Oh, man.

00:01:47.724 --> 00:01:48.975
- I don't even think you
could eat a whole bag,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.429
'cause you eat one, you're just like...

00:01:52.187 --> 00:01:53.522
- It's like a task.

00:01:53.522 --> 00:01:54.940
- KuSuka chips.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.274
Also the same as crack cocaine.

00:01:56.274 --> 00:01:57.567
- Indestructable.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:58.610
That's weird.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:00.862
- This glaze is made out
of polymer, isn't it?

00:02:00.862 --> 00:02:03.574
That's like the secret? It's plastic.

00:02:04.956 --> 00:02:06.702
- Kukagumi!

00:02:06.702 --> 00:02:09.913
Which is a fresh, daily snacks.

00:02:09.913 --> 00:02:11.843
- I bet these make you (beep) a brick.

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:14.835
